{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple indirect routes. The first pathway links Cassialactone to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is then targeted by (4S,4aR,5S,8aR,9aS)-4a,5,6,7,8,8a,9,9a-Octahydro-4-hydroxy-9a-methoxy-3,4a,5-trimethylnaphtho(2,3-b)furan-2(4H)-one, a compound that ultimately targets Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. In a separate pathway, Cassialactone directly targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is subsequently targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which also targets the same kinase. These findings suggest that Cassialactone may influence the activity of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through distinct but related molecular mechanisms, potentially involving different substrates and downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a broad role for Cassialactone in modulating this kinase, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
